--TEST--
`if (...): … endif;` is not syntax, so the `:` and `endif` are refused as an expression that is not there, and what survives is coloured as the loose statements the parser recovered rather than as a block — `rule:ide/rejected-syntax-gets-no-colour`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Real {}
var $n = 1;
if ($n):
    $n = 2;
endif;
var $b = 3;
--REQUEST--
semanticTokens
--EXPECT--
2:7+4 class
3:5+2 variable
4:5+2 variable
5:5+2 variable
7:5+2 variable
